From a28e9a3c584b6529578ad9416fa9ca0591e70ff1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:23:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 191/192] clk: mediatek: transfer MT6897 OVL boot votes after
 off epochs

Add a single-controller boot-owner handle for the static built-in top
provider. Resolve the bound provider under its device lock, validate the
explicit voted OVL mux IDs and retain its device reference. Publish private
state only after successful clock-provider setup and suppress unbind.

Serialize enable/disable ownership and live state with off-epoch accounting
under one IRQ-safe lock. Require the classified ordinary roots to be live
before recording an epoch. OVL1's epoch permits its functional root;
both sticky epochs permit shared OVL0. Transfer only inherited/owned
accounting, without CCF/PM calls or SET/CLR writes. Ordinary last disable
performs release and retains retry state on unvote failure.

Add portable enrollment, predicate, ordering, retry and shared-lock tests,
including shared-bank bit preservation. These host tests do not establish
hardware timing or kernel lockdep behavior.
